    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Prove that the sum of five consecutive integers is a multiple of 5.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$5(n+2)$, where $n$ is the first integer.\n\nCollect the five terms and factor out 5.",
      "worked": "Let $n$ be the first integer and $S$ their sum.\n$$\\begin{align*}S &= n+(n+1)+(n+2)+(n+3)+(n+4)\\\\S &= 5n+(1+2+3+4)\\\\S &= 5n+10\\\\S &= 5(n+2).\\end{align*}$$\nSince $n+2$ is an integer, the sum is a multiple of 5.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
  },
